    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.Programs.Allow">Let the agent run programs</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.Programs.Allow.Hint">Off, the agent can only read and change files. On, it can also build the project, run its tests and ask version control what changed - which is what lets it find out whether an edit actually works.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.Programs.Warning.Title">A program is not confined to the project folder</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.Programs.Warning.Message">It runs as you, so it can reach the network, the rest of the disk and anything your account can open. Every single command is put to you for approval first, with the program and each argument shown in full, and that approval is never remembered - ten commands is ten questions. There is no shell, so nothing in a command can chain a second one.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.Programs.List">Programs the agent may run</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.Programs.List.Hint">Separated by commas or spaces, and by name only - 'dotnet', never a path to it. Capitals and a trailing .exe are ignored. Anything not on this list is refused, and the agent is told to ask you rather than look for another way.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.Programs.List.ShellWarning">Adding a shell - cmd, powershell, pwsh, bash, wsl - allows every program on the machine through it, and makes the rest of this list decorative.</sys:String>
